A||||22||86SE||I was just in a bad accident.............||||11||
Z||000000||86SE||05-23-2001||10:20 PM||||Last Thursday some friends and I were out crusing around in a another friend's Jeep Cherokee.  We were going to hop in the Fiero because school just got out but we said we will just cruise in the Jeep for a few minutes like we do everyday after school.  I get in the back seat of the Jeep on the drivers side.  The driver was Jeremy, passenger in the front seat was Dusty, in the back seat it was me, behind the driver, then Micah in the middle, then Snoozy behind the passenger seat.  I get in a put my seat belt on (wore it ever since the roll over accident Micah and I were in 3 weeks earlier).  Were drivin for about 5 minutes befor we start to head out of town.  We get off the highway and start to speed up as we get out of town.  A car up the road stops for the stop sign, then creeps very slowly in to the intersection, then STOPS 3/4 in our lane and completely filling the other lane!  No way we could have made it by swerving behind them, so we have to swerve in front of them.  We are doing about 55-60 when we hit the ditch.  I remember Dusty yelling to Jeremy "Don't hit that pole!"  we ramp out of the ditch when we hit a median, fly over 6 feet in the air and 45 feet long when we crash into a 1.5 foot in diameter utility pole.  My face hit the back of the drivers seat and my head bent way back.<P>I was the only one not knocked unconcious. As soon as the Jeep stoped moving I jumped out of the window.  Blood war streaming down my face so I checked my head to see if it was cracked open because it was numb.  I was relieved when I found it was just coming from my nearly broken nose.  I run around to the other side of the Jeep to check on the others.  I see Snoozy with his back arched over the seat yelling in pain, I thought he broke his back.  I look at Micah who is twitching on the seat where I was sitting with blood being spit from his mouth.  I look in the front seat to see just a tiny smashed in space where my friend Dusty was.  Dusty was knocked out cramed in with his feet above his head (his feet were on the dash).  Jeremy was unconcious leaning on the stering wheel.  I ran to the shop to get help, jumping over the downed power lines.<P>I get back to the scene and there were a ton of people there just watching.  Dusty got out on his own, yelling and kicking on the ground.  Jeremy and Micah were out sitting on the ground, and Snoozy was still in the Jeep holding his broken arm.<P>We all went to hospitals as soon as ambulances arrived.  Dusty and Jeremy were air lifted to Sioux Falls.  Micah, Snoozy and I went to Mitchell.  I had x-rays taken of my neck (pretty bad whip lash) and released 2 hours later.  Snoozy just had a broken arm and he was out the nexy day.  Micah was transfered from Mitchell to Sioux Falls 3 hours after he got to the hospital.  Micah had his upper and lower jaws broke along with his right eye socket.  Jeremy broke his clavicle, shoulder blade and 4 ribs and was out the next day.  Dusty bruised his lungs and broke 3 vertebra in his lumbar region.<P>Dusty and Micah were in the intensive care for almost a week (they got out today).  They both still lay in the hospital awaiting any necessicary surgury.<P>No one is paralized, but they are all hurt, some worse then others.  Micah's face looks pretty bad but both Dusty and Micah should be out soon.<P>That was my accident, its kinda long but a seatbelt saved my from being seriously hurt, so this has taught me to ALWAYS wear my seatbelt.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||11
Z||000001||mrgone||05-23-2001||10:24 PM||||always have always will<P>except on the beach||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||05-23-2001||10:25 PM||||Don't be foolish, wear it all the time, small fender benders can be the cause of major whiplash or injury!  <P>Wear it ALWAYS - Even on the beach - Safety IS in style||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||05-23-2001||10:26 PM||||Wow! <BR>keep wearing it, it works<BR>hope you and your friends get back to 100%||||reg||11
Z||000004||wkayl||05-24-2001||12:56 AM||||Seatbelts save my son and I last fall...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/OOPS_1.jpg">  <P>And when a guy ran a stop sign and hit him a year ago last January...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/caseycrash.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 05-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Neverfinished||05-24-2001||01:02 AM||||i'm glad everyones ok. I've had too many friends die in accidents that could have been prevented with a seatbelt. <BR>It's good to hear you are ok and I hope your friends get better soon.<BR>ps. Be very thankful you weren't driving your fiero.<P>------------------<BR>To Be Old And Wise, You First Must Be Young And Stupid.-----------------<BR>It's not a waste of time... If you are wasted at the time||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||05-24-2001||03:36 AM||||geez! I'm glad you're alright..... I hope your friends get better soon....<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||8
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||05-24-2001||04:09 AM||||Wow... I'm just glad you are still here to tell us about it...||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroHarry||05-24-2001||06:41 AM||||Sound like somebody upstairs was looking out for you guy's <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Best wishes to you all!<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||6
Z||000009||Raydar||05-24-2001||10:42 AM||||I glad you didn't get hurt any worse than you did. Hopefully your friends will recover quickly.<BR>I always wear a seatbelt. Ever since one stopped me from eating a steering wheel. <P>You didn't say, but I'm guessing the other car didn't stick around...<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000010||grinthock||05-24-2001||11:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Wow... I'm just glad you are still here to tell us about it...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>yes - and I am also glad this forum is still here for you to tell us about it....<P>(Ok that was a bad A** Kissing.... Soemone help!! It's SUCKING ME IN!!!! I AM STUCK!!!)||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ken Wittlief||05-24-2001||11:08 AM||||FieroHarry: ?!?!? If thats the best that 'someone upstairs' can do to look out for us then we need to get someone else upstairs!<P>   How bout next time we get a booming voice 20 seconds before the accident that says "STOP!" or a gentle hand that pulls our brake pedal down ahead of time so the accident doenst happen?<P>  Or a big hand that pushes the other car out of the way, or lifts our car up and gently sets us back down on the other side. That would be a miracle!<P>   God has given us the absolute freedom of choice to govern our own lives AND the terrible responsibility that goes with it. Please dont go around thinking that if someone else is careless or makes a mistake that God is gonna step in and take that freedom or responsibility away from them, or step in to save us from their carelessness either.<P> that is a terrible philosophy to go through life with. And what does it say about the people that die in accidents, God wasnt interested in looking out for them?<P>Everytime we get in a car we are taking a risk - and we are vunerable to other drivers mistakes. You have to be aware of that - dont expect divine intervention to save you.<P> What happened to the car that caused the accident? did they flee the scene? were they cited? Arrested?<P>  This is a grim reminder that our ability to move around at highway speeds is a very dangerous aspect of modern life - at any given time on the road we are only inches away, seconds away, or one mistake away from possible injury or death - and it doesnt have to be your mistake or fault.<P>   This accident touches on one of the things that drives me nuts, people that inch out from side streets while you are coming down the road, and you have the right of way. They inch out a little bit, or start pulling out before you have even reached the intersection. You dont know if they are only moving up a foot, or if they dont see you at all. Whenever someone does this to me they get a good long blast from my horn - or better yet, I slam on the brakes and screech to a stop if Im really not sure if they see me or not - then I sit there for 10 or 20 seconds and stare them down.<P>   this habit of people creeping up on side streets is getting to be more and more of a problem, and this accident is why - if the car does not sit dead still till you pass by, you cant tell what the driver is thinking, seeing, or doing.<P>  We need to make creeping up at an intersection a moving violation, just like running a red light. We have enough stress in driving already without having to deal with this nonsense at every intersection. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Ken Wittlief||05-24-2001||11:14 AM||||FieroHarry - sorry for jumping on your case - it drives me nuts when there is a tragic accident, esp when people die, and someone survives and people say "it was a miracle he survived"<BR>  <BR>  NO! it would be a miracle if the accident didnt happen in the first place.<P>   Just a pet peeve with me - sorry to take it out on you!<P>  -Ken||||reg||1
Z||000013||grinthock||05-24-2001||11:19 AM||||Well laws in Canada state.<P>You must come to a complete stop at a stop sign before proceeding.  <P>You must stop either at the line, if no line, then the edge ofthe sidewalk, if no sidewalk at the edge of the road.<P>Proceed when clear and safe.<P>IF people stopped in the right spot, it would be CLEAR if they were proceeding or not.  IF they inch ahead then go it's a rolling stop.  If they stop completly, then being to just roll without proceeding it's ALSO a rolling stop.<P>AND in Ontario rolling Stop == running a stop which = $210 fine and 2 points.<P>so basically it IS illegal here to do that crap, BUT it's never actually enforced (excluding complete rolling stops where the person never stops)<P>IF people stopped at the EDGE of the road where you are supposed to then it would be obvious because there is no room to creep or roll||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ken Wittlief||05-24-2001||11:31 AM||||exactly! and if they are stopped and they see you coming then they have NO reason to creep forward - cause you are coming and they cant go yet. once the way is clear - then if they still cant see THEN they can move up some and take another look.<P>  Its a simple matter of rudeness and being inconsiderate - they dont care if they are making your job harder. Esp the ones that are pulling in from the left side of the road and start BEFORE you even get to the intersection! Almost everytime this happens I nail the brakes - I have no way of telling if he is gonna punch the gas and pull in front of me, or if hes gonna broadside me.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Ken Wittlief||05-24-2001||11:42 AM||||86SE: the best advice I can give you is what someone told me when I learned to drive a motorcycle in florida. When you drive a motorcycle assume you are completely INVISABLE and nobody can see you - be prepaired for people to pull out in front of you and always have an escape path planned in your head, before it happens.<P>  In a car its not that bad, but always assume the other driver is totally inept, stupid, will do the worst thing, and be ready for it. this can be as simple as taking your foot off the gas and holding it over the brake at all intersections, or actually slowing down when someone is waiting to pull out onto your road.<P>   Assume the other person is full of Nyquil PM and you will be ready for anything.<P>  I had a plumbers truck back out into the street right infront of me once. I thought he would stop at the curb but he kept right on going. I had to slam on the brakes to avoid hitting him, and i laid on the horn, and started rolling down the window to cuss him out<P>  there was nobody to cuss out. There was nobody in the truck - it had rolled down the driveway all by itself.<P>   So better yet, assume the other driver is totally not there - physically, mentally - whatever. most of the time its not true - but all it takes is for it to be true once. then all that carefull driving, all the times you put your foot over the brake or slowed up a little - all that previous effort will pay off big time on that ONE occasion when you really do need it.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 05-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Ken Wittlief||05-24-2001||11:48 AM||||86SE: BTW I know you werent driving when this accident happened, but I am sure you and your friends will talk about it and go over it from time to time. A bad experience like this is the most expensive teacher - Im sure you will all take the most you can from it.||||reg||1
Z||000017||84Bill||05-24-2001||11:59 AM||||A similer thing happend to me while I was riding my cycle (3 days old) A guy suddenly came to a stop to make a left turn blocking all avenues of avoidence. since I was riding the inner portion of the lane, I swerved to the left to try and get around the front of him only to have him hear screaching brakes and blairing horn, he mashed it and I waffeled the front just behind the tire. My only thaught was "wow I'm gonna die" as I sailed 40 feet beyond the car and hit the ground only to slide another 15 feet. I could not believe I was able to walk away with only minor road rash. but another 2 feet back and I would have hit the door post and well lets say I shudder to think about it. Had I went around the rear I would not have not made it either according to the police. I was cited for improper passing and was happy to be alive to pay it.||||reg||14
Z||000018||stsmithgt||05-24-2001||03:00 PM||||I've been plowed into by someone running red light before.  It changed my attitude towards those law breakers.  I don't roll stop signs though I may anticipate a light.  If I have no place to go around them without destroying my car, I'm taking them with me! Hello! welcome to my world! BAM!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Why should one have the pain and expense of an accident and the dope get off scott free most likely without a even ticket.(bitter boy attitude sneaking out).  The screwed part of that attitude would be if it was an old person or kids in the other vehicle.  Thank god(or somebody) the Fiero can dodge several kinds of bad cituations to avoid using that negative attitude. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I don't like those automatic seat belts some cars have.  I'd have the fear of being trapped.  I like having the choice though I wear the belt 99.9% of the time.  It's better then smacking the steering wheel with your chest or face.<P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||Ken Wittlief||05-24-2001||03:19 PM||||Keep a knife handy in your car all the time, where you can reach it easily, one you can open with one hand if you are all banged up. Being strapped in and unable to get out is one of my fears for accidents.<P>  or worst yet you come across an accident and someone cant get out when they need do - I also keep a fire extinquisher in all my cars (am I an overgrown boyscout or what?)<P>  maybe I shouldnt say this about accidents, but if you hit someone, and your car hits straight on and stays straight, the damage to your person will be much lower then if you hit something else with a glancing blow.<P>  Seatbelts, headrests and airbags protect you most in the front and rear direction.<P>   so whats the big deal? if you see an accident coming, and you try to avoid it, and dont make it all the way, and catch the other car with 1/4 of your bumper, or you slid sideways because you oversteered, then when you hit your car is gonna spin around violently - most likely snapping your neck or putting your vehicle occupants heads through the side windows.<P>   That is an awesome snap decision to have to make, should I brake hard but stay pointed straight at the other car, or should I try to swerve to avoid the other car, and maybe kill myself if I dont make it all the way clear and just catch the corner of it?<P>  we need something on the outside of our cars like that mars rover had when it landed, giant outside airbags that inflate and surround the whole car.<P>   An accident is a bad deal all the way around. I think the only time you can avoid one with a conscious decision taking place is when you loose your brakes or something like that, and you have a few seconds to decide what you want to hit to stop your car. In that case, sliding along a guard rail or a wall is better than hitting another car. But usually the only response you make at all is a snap reflex.||||reg||1
Z||000020||coolcat||05-24-2001||05:20 PM||||always wear your seatbelt if my friend who was sitting shotgun wasnt wearing hers the said that she would have been killed .so always wear it <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/scan2_4.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/scan2_4.JPG</A> <P>------------------<BR>Gettin good players is easy,gettin them to play together is the hard part||||reg||14
Z||000021||86SE||05-27-2001||03:39 AM||||I just need to say there must have been some body watching out for us.  Heres why, usually after school the drive, Jermey, and I are the first ones out the door so I usually ride shotgun.  But THIS time, and only this time, Dusty was out the door first and he called shotgun before Snoozy.  This is also a first when Snoozy dident call shotgun before Dusty. I dont know why, but thats what happened.  And for some reason Micah and I were the LAST ones out of school.  Micah followed me out the door and we walked over to the Jeep.  I see that Dusty is already in the front so I cant get in the front.  Then I open Snoozy's door, he says "Get in the other door, I aint scootin over"  Micah was behind me, so when we both turn around, Micah was in front of me.  Micah opens the back door on the drivers side and we both get in.  So right there I should have been in the passenger seat up front, but Dusty was there.  Should have gotten in Snoozy's seat, but Snoozy wouldent scoot over.  And I should have been sitting in the middle and have the smashed up face that Micah has now, but I didnt.<P>And something else that I found was really weird and also tells me some one was looking out for me was that the only seatbelt in the back that could have been used was the one on the drivers side, the side I was sitting on.  Because the back seats in jeeps flap up, and when you pull them up all the seatbelt clasps (where they connect) fall into the seat and when you fold the seat back down you cant get to the parts where you fasten the seatbelts.  The middle seatbelt was completely under the seat so there is no way that one could have been used.<P>So right when I got in, I put my seatbelt on.  And not even 1 minute before the accident Dusty lit up his ciggarette.  And when he lights up a ciggarette he tends to put his feet up on the dash so he can rest his arm on his leg while he smokes.  He kept his feet up on the dash suring the accident and thats what actually saved his life.  If not his life, at least his legs.  The passenger compartment was completely smashed in.  The front end was crushed so much that the engine took up the ENTIRE foot well of the passenger compartment.  His legs would have been crushed to about his hips.  So if I was in front not even a seatbelt whould have saved my legs, cuz I never put my feet up on the dash.<P>Mabey all this is just one big coincidence how all this was set up.  There is even a lot more stuff that happened in those few minutes that makes me think someone higher up is keeping on eye out for us but I dont feel like typing it all.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg"> <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *SUSPENDED* --<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
Z||000022||86SE||07-17-2001||02:08 AM||||I found the old post.....now this pic goes with the above story.....<P> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/Jeep/jeep2.jpg"> ||||reg||3
